  a lot I smuggled cameras into eastern  Germany my friends took off the secret  police and climbed the lights in church  [Applause]  the army had taken up positions in the  side streets backed up by tanks East  Germany was on the verge of civil war  for some reason we were pushed to the  front to the front row that hasn't been  our plan when the protest march started  we linked arms as we had seen people do  in the movies we thought that's just  what you do  but after a while we realized that the  police and the army we're not  intervening they just let us march the  next day footage shot by Roland's  friends ended up on the West German news  it became obvious East Germany's days  were numbered  journalists were part from reporting  from Nasik  protesters didn't know foreign reporters  could capture this footage 70,000 took  to the streets one of the first East  German leaders to fall was Irish mukha  head of the secret police the Stasi from  his headquarters he had overseen a vast  informers Network never would he have  imagined that his office would one day  be a tourist attraction he used this  safe to store compromising documents on  East German leader Erich Honecker one  card is no standing in Irish milkers  former headquarters makes clear just  what great symbolic meaning this has we  have visitors from 40 different  countries who admire Germany for having  toppled the dictatorship and for being  this brave it sends a strong signal and  creates home today Roland Yan is in  charge of East Germany Stasi files he  shows us the cellar where there are  endless rows of them Germany was able to  salvage most of them making them  accessible to former victims of the East  German regime andreas Rost appreciates  this former East German Communist Party  members and informers were not treated  with leniency after the fall of the wall  but he thinks other big mistakes were  made to this day many East Germans feel  they are not treated equally and he says  it was recognized too late that eastern  Germany has a problem with right-wing  extremism and xenophobia Jesus musn't  this for at first we chanted we are the  people then we are one people okay which  is still acceptable but when this change  into the belief that foreigners should  leave Germany something definitely went  wrong the Berlin Wall came down 30 years  ago but to this day the country still  isn't truly United that will take more  than one generation  [Music]

